    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"polarity\",\n      \"components\": [\"D1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"D1.1\", \"D1.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"GND\", \"TACH\"],\n      \"observed\": \"D1 (5V1 Zener, Device:D_Zener_Small) has its cathode (pin 1, K) on GND and its anode (pin 2, A) on TACH. The Zener is therefore oriented to clamp TACH on its negative swing, not its positive swing. A positive TACH level forward-biases it at roughly 0.6\u20130.7 V.\",\n      \"expected\": \"A 5.1 V Zener used as an over-voltage clamp on the TACH sense line should have its cathode on TACH and its anode on GND, so that it only conducts above about 5.1 V. As drawn, the part would clamp the tach pulses (pulled up through R6 to VCC) to about 0.7 V.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"D1 | 5V1 | Diode_SMD:D_SOD-123 | Device:D_Zener_Small | Zener diode, small symbol\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"GND : C1.2(passive) C2.2(passive) D1.1(K,passive)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"TACH : D1.2(A,passive) R4.1(passive) R6.2(passive) U2.3(XTAL2/PB4,bidirectional) U3.3(PB4,bidirectional)\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The TACH input would be held near 0.7 V whenever the fan's tach output tries to go high. The ATtiny tach-read logic would see a degraded or missing pulse train, so fan speed sensing would fail.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.6\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist's fan-controller design shows a Zener D1 wired with its cathode on GND and its anode on the TACH line, which is reversed for an over-voltage clamp and would clamp the tach signal near 0.7 V. The rest of the connectivity and values appear consistent, and the specification describes an unrelated repository, so it provides no direct check on this board.\"\n}",
